## Routing user asks → PipeCrew skills

| The user wants… | Use |
|---|---|
| A feature shipped end-to-end across repos (requirements → design → implementation → review) | `/pipecrew:deliver <description>` |
| A small, well-specified mechanical change (audit fix, codemod, convention sweep) | `/pipecrew:patch` — bounce to `/deliver` if it grows requirements or contract changes |
| A bug or incident investigated from a symptom (read-only triage) | `/pipecrew:troubleshoot <symptom>` |
| A branch or PR reviewed in one repo | `/pipecrew:review` |
| A feature branch's cross-repo integration verified | `/pipecrew:assess` |
| Feedback (merged PR, run, session, notes) captured into durable conventions | `/pipecrew:learn` |
| Ideas — what to build next, or how to build it | `/pipecrew:brainstorm` (`--technical` for solution approaches) |
| Context docs audited or refreshed after code drift | `/pipecrew:context-refresh` |
| Architecture diagrams generated or refreshed | `/pipecrew:draw-diagram` |
| Acceptance test cases authored — baseline suite for existing features, or covering a past /deliver run | `/pipecrew:design-tests` |
| A new project onboarded, or repos added to a workspace | `/pipecrew:discover` |
| A teammate onboarded onto an existing workspace | `/pipecrew:join <memory-repo-url>` |
| Shared team memory inspected or synced now | `/pipecrew:memory-sync status \| pull \| sync` |

## Dispatching agents directly (without a skill)

Skills orchestrate multi-agent pipelines; for a single consultation, analysis, or report, dispatch the agent itself with the Agent tool (`subagent_type` below). The `<slug>-*` agents are the workspace's own — use the concrete names listed in each workspace block above.

| Need | Agent (`subagent_type`) |
|---|---|
| Technical design or architecture opinion | `pipecrew:solution-architect` (`MODE: brainstorm` for consultations) |
| Product requirements (FR/EC) from a feature idea | `<slug>-product-owner` |
| Read-only incident triage report | `<slug>-troubleshooter` |
| Cross-repo quality assessment of a branch | `<slug>-assessor` |
| UX recommendation + implementation spec for a frontend | `pipecrew:ux-consultant` |
| Security review of a design or a diff | `pipecrew:security-consultant` |
| CLAUDE.md / agent-context generation or refresh for a repo | `pipecrew:context-manager` |
| Code-grounded architecture diagrams | `pipecrew:architecture-mapper` |
| Run execution report (timeline, tokens, cost) | `pipecrew:reporter` |
| Product ideation partner (greenfield or feature) | `pipecrew:product-brainstormer` |

Workspace-local stack agents (`<slug>-<type>-implementer` / `<slug>-<type>-reviewer`) may also exist for stacks the plugin doesn't ship. Prefer the skills for implementation work — they wire in spec edits, worktrees, and paired review rounds that a lone agent dispatch skips.
